  message: "Materialized from dogfood tranche 05 (F93.A1 / anon-card-017). Mechanism: containment-linker confidence direction anti-correlated with mechanism reliability (naming_convention heuristic@1.0 outranks span_overlap certain@0.9). Evidence: frozen substrate.json (probe_1_contains_conf.log) buckets (1.0,naming_convention)=18388 / (0.9,span_overlap)=4471; producer linkers/containment.py phases 1/1.5/2 read in live repo. Magnitude: 30 provably-false class->method contains at confidence 1.0 (re-derived count 30, not 28) — method spans lying outside the class span in the same file; concrete _FakeMetadata @ test_analyzer_identity.py:205-207 'contains' methods at 234-235/270-271. Blind severity 4/5, reproduced on frozen substrate. RELATED_BUT_DISTINCT from WI-lutad (18388 linker edges exceed 0.95 ceiling — that's about linker edge confidence breaching the ceiling generally; this is the DIRECTION of the hardcoding being anti-correlated with truth, and the 1.0 bucket is exactly the contains/naming_convention phase), WI-suvil (confidence hardcoded not evidence-derived — META parent), and the ledger same-base-name misattribution row F81.A1/WI-jafat (same root naming mechanism, but here the wrong edge carries the MAXIMUM confidence 1.0)."  # f1c3
